        <mxCell id="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-18" edge="1" parent="1" source="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-6" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" target="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-9" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-19" edge="1" parent="1" source="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-7" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" target="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-8" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-20" edge="1" parent="1" source="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-7" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" target="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-9" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-21" edge="1" parent="1" source="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-6" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=0.96;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-10" value="writes images today">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-22" edge="1" parent="1" source="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-6" style="endArrow=open;endFill=0;dashed=1;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=11;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-11" value="upload  (planned)">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="59XLJyg0iTgdv8digokF-23" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" value="Four things this diagram states:&lt;br&gt;1. The API keeps NO state, so it can be replicated. Everything that used to&lt;br&gt;   live in process memory — cache, rate-limit counters, socket lists — is in Redis.&lt;br&gt;   PARTLY TRUE NOW (Epic 4): the catalog cache IS externalisable to Redis via&lt;br&gt;   REDIS_URL (single-flight + fail-open) and @keyv/redis is a dependency, so a&lt;br&gt;   shared cache across replicas works. STILL IN-PROCESS: ThrottlerModule rate-&lt;br&gt;   limit counters and the websocket socket lists — so the API is not yet fully&lt;br&gt;   stateless and the x3 above remains a target for those two pieces.&lt;br&gt;2. Exactly ONE worker. Cron inside the API would run the reconciliation job&lt;br&gt;   three times; for a job that touches money that is a serious bug.&lt;br&gt;   NOT TRUE YET: TasksModule is imported by AppModule, so the cron runs inside&lt;br&gt;   the API. Harmless while there is one replica — and the exact reason a second&lt;br&gt;   replica cannot simply be started.&lt;br&gt;3. Images ARE on the VPS disk today — multer writes to public/images/{folder},&lt;br&gt;   and there is no R2 or S3 client anywhere in src/. That blocks point 1: a&lt;br&gt;   second API replica cannot serve an image the first one wrote. Moving to R2&lt;br&gt;   is decided, not built.&lt;br&gt;4. Admin is its own deployable on its own hostname, so admin code is never&lt;br&gt;   shipped in the customer bundle. Sessions are per-origin, so an admin who&lt;br&gt;   also sells signs in twice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checked against the code on 14/08/2026. Red = decided, not built.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The box is now buildable. Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml exist in&lt;br&gt;Zoldify_Backend; an earlier mysql+migrate+api stack was brought up from an&lt;br&gt;empty volume and answered on /api/v1/products. Compose now ALSO declares a&lt;br&gt;redis service and passes REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379 to the api, so Redis&lt;br&gt;backs the catalog cache (Epic 4). Honest caveat: the redis-included compose&lt;br&gt;is config-verified (YAML + wiring) but NOT yet brought up — the author box&lt;br&gt;has no Docker. Still no worker.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The uploads question has an answer now: compose mounts a NAMED volume at&lt;br&gt;/app/public/images, and a file written there survives docker compose down and&lt;br&gt;up — measured, not assumed. That keeps uploads across a redeploy but does not&lt;br&gt;unblock point 1: a volume lives on one machine, so it still cannot be shared&lt;br&gt;by two API replicas. Only object storage fixes that.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;See DEPLOY.md for the commands and for what is still missing." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="480" width="740" x="70" y="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
