        <mxCell id="aiQKo2CWYi5a2MvuZvO3-17" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" value="Arrows point DOWNWARD only. Identity is the foundation and depends on nobody.&lt;br&gt;Money depends only on Identity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Money must NOT point at Ordering. Ordering computes the amount and calls Money,&lt;br&gt;passing a reference like {type: order, id: 123}. To Money that reference is an&lt;br&gt;opaque string — it does not know what an order is. That is what makes Money the&lt;br&gt;easiest context to split into its own service later.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The rule is enforced by eslint-plugin-boundaries, not by convention. Current&lt;br&gt;debt: 29 legacy violations, allowed to shrink but never to grow." vertex="1">
