        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wzBXlo48OZKu_Q5dPZ6v-32" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" value="The three orange gates are what makes the architecture hold over time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;boundaries:check turns the context dependency rule from a spoken agreement&lt;br&gt;into a merge blocker. Without it the rule is broken within two weeks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;openapi:check guarantees web and mobile never build against a stale contract.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;diagrams:check means a broken diagram cannot be merged — the report depends&lt;br&gt;on them rendering.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;NOT BUILT YET: the backend has no .github/workflows at all. This is B, week 1." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="620" x="70" y="430" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wzBXlo48OZKu_Q5dPZ6v-33" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" value="The red column is a plan, not a description&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;There is no Dockerfile and no compose file in any of the four repositories.&lt;br&gt;The only container in the project is started by scripts/test-db.mjs with a&lt;br&gt;bare `docker run mysql:8` for the test database.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml now exist, and `docker compose up -d --build`&lt;br&gt;has been run from an empty volume: 25 tables migrated, both containers healthy,&lt;br&gt;/api/v1/products answering. So the migration step is real and is drawn black.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The two boxes still red need things that do not exist: there is no&lt;br&gt;.github/workflows anywhere, so nothing builds or pushes an image; and there is&lt;br&gt;no VPS to ssh into. Until then a deploy is `git pull` then `npm run docker:up`&lt;br&gt;on the machine itself, which builds locally and skips GHCR entirely." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="620" x="70" y="620" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="wzBXlo48OZKu_Q5dPZ6v-34" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" value="This pipeline runs per repository. Four repositories:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Zoldify_Backend    lint · boundaries:check · test · build · openapi:check · diagrams:check&lt;br&gt;Zoldify_Frontend   lint · build · gen:api must match the committed schema&lt;br&gt;Zoldify_Admin      lint · build · check-shared must match Zoldify_Frontend   (planned)&lt;br&gt;Zoldify_Mobile     lint · typecheck · EAS build&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;check-shared is the gate specific to the admin split: the modules copied from&lt;br&gt;the shop repo must stay byte-identical. Without it the two copies drift, which&lt;br&gt;is exactly how the order-status table ended up with four versions." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="620" x="70" y="800" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
